1
00:00:00,630 --> 00:00:03,510
[SORGHAGHTANI] Fatima...
I want you...

2
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:06,930
to act as a spy for me.

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:08,590
♪

4
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,350
A spy?

5
00:00:11,810 --> 00:00:12,970
Hmm.

6
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:18,900
As you must know, Brother Ögedei
has taken the throne as emperor.

7
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:23,230
Both Tolui and I are willing
to accept this outcome...

8
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,860
if all goes well.

9
00:00:24,990 --> 00:00:26,320
That said,

10
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:30,070
the bond between brothers
is quite a fragile thing.

11
00:00:31,030 --> 00:00:34,790
Despite being passed over,
Tolui, as the Otchigin,

12
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:38,290
now wields the most
military power in the empire.

13
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,250
Left alone, I'm concerned

14
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:43,210
that this imbalance
will only bring misfortune.

15
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:45,590
[Sitara grunts]

16
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:48,880
I think I'm beginning
to understand.

17
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:51,260
So what is it you want me
to do then?

18
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:55,600
Insinuate yourself
into Brother Chagatai's court

19
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,060
and report his movements
in detail.

20
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,640
Prince Chagatai?

21
00:00:59,770 --> 00:01:03,110
Indeed. Let us assume
the very worst.

22
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:07,740
If anybody were to come between
the Great Kha'an and Tolui,

23
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,610
it would be none other
than Brother Chagatai,

24
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:14,410
for he's always been closest
to Brother Ögedei.

25
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:18,040
I know you're someone
he would never suspect

26
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:19,460
since you've never met.

27
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:23,460
For our sake, you'll agree
to carry this out, won't you?

28
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:25,590
[gasps softly]

29
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:30,090
[♪ opening theme song playing]

30
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:08,310
[SORGHAGHTANI]
Tomorrow morning,

31
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,900
head to the tent
that's marked with a flag.

32
00:03:11,030 --> 00:03:13,740
Then you'll be told
how to go undercover.

33
00:03:14,490 --> 00:03:17,910
[SITARA] That tent,
it has a flag right outside.

34
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:19,660
Must be it then.

35
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:23,580
But now that I've arrived,
what am I supposed to do?

36
00:03:23,710 --> 00:03:25,290
-[SHIRA] Fatima!
-Hmm?

37
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:30,550
Hey.

38
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:33,090
Shira? Is that you?

39
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:36,130
I can hardly recognize you
as a grown man.

40
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:38,260
What brings you
all the way out here?

41
00:03:38,390 --> 00:03:40,510
I thought you were employed
by Prince Tolui.

42
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,060
[Shira laughs]

43
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:44,020
His consort,
Princess Sorghaghtani,

44
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,270
came asking for me,

45
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:47,230
so now I'm here
to try and help you.

46
00:03:47,350 --> 00:03:48,310
Oh.

47
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:49,770
And besides,

48
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,480
it sounds like the winds
of change are finally blowing.

49
00:03:52,610 --> 00:03:54,780
[in deep voice] This could be
our big chance to succeed.

50
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:56,570
Seems you're the same as ever.

51
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:59,620
-So, what's inside that tent?
-Huh?

52
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:03,540
[SHIRA] Oh, that belongs
to the lost property officer.

53
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:05,370
It's where all
the unclaimed cattle

54
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:07,420
and slaves are kept
for safekeeping.

55
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,460
After the autumn move
and the Kurultai,

56
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:12,000
I imagine things
are pretty hectic.

57
00:04:15,170 --> 00:04:16,760
The idea is to exploit that

58
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:19,180
and have you replace one
of Prince Chagatai's slaves.

59
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,680
So I'll be swapping places
with someone then?

60
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,060
Do you really believe
we'll find a slave

61
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:26,190
who resembles me so easily?

62
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:29,110
Uh...

63
00:04:30,190 --> 00:04:33,230
Yeah, of course I do,
if the stars so will it.

64
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,570
-Come on, let's go.
-Uh?

65
00:04:36,030 --> 00:04:37,740
[grunts nervously]

66
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:39,450
[sighs]

67
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:42,280
I'm getting the feeling
this won't end well.

68
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:46,620
-Please excuse me, my good sir.
-Hmm?

69
00:04:46,750 --> 00:04:49,500
I came across a slave
who's gotten lost.

70
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,710
Could I leave her with you?

71
00:04:51,790 --> 00:04:52,840
[SITARA] Uh...

72
00:04:53,550 --> 00:04:56,340
Is there anything
that might help identify her?

73
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:58,510
[SHIRA]
Well, I couldn't really say.

74
00:04:58,630 --> 00:05:01,220
Uh, she seems no different
from any of the others.

75
00:05:01,350 --> 00:05:02,300
[Sitara chuckles]

76
00:05:02,430 --> 00:05:04,430
You see? She has
a friendly smile,

77
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,850
but apart from that,
she's quite unremarkable, yes?

78
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:08,690
Hey! What's that about?

79
00:05:08,810 --> 00:05:10,440
Hey, don't get so upset with me.

80
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,310
This will be easier
if you don't stand out.

81
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:14,570
You didn't have to say it
like that though.

82
00:05:14,690 --> 00:05:16,190
[SHIRA]
There, there. [laughs nervously]

83
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:19,240
Oh? You just dropped something.

84
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:21,030
[both gasp]

85
00:05:22,570 --> 00:05:23,740
What is that thing?

86
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:26,950
[SITARA]
This is called a bezoar stone.

87
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:29,210
It was in some sheep entrails.

88
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:32,580
Oh! That can cure things, right?
I've heard of it.

89
00:05:32,710 --> 00:05:35,920
Hmm? Hold on there.
That's a Jada stone, isn't it?

90
00:05:36,050 --> 00:05:36,960
[Sitara gasps]

91
00:05:37,550 --> 00:05:40,260
I have never heard it
referred to as a "bezoar."

92
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,970
When we see a stone formed
inside of an animal,

93
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:44,350
it is called a "Jada."

94
00:05:44,470 --> 00:05:46,180
They're used
to help summon rain.

95
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,640
When a kam soaks one in water...

96
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:02,780
it is said to immediately
bring forth a mighty rainstorm.

97
00:06:02,910 --> 00:06:05,330
How did a slave like you
find such a thing?

98
00:06:05,450 --> 00:06:06,580
Huh?

99
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:08,410
[SITARA] Maybe bringing this
along with me

100
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:09,910
wasn't a good idea.

101
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:11,500
I, uh...

102
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:14,750
Oh, that's right.
It was meant for my master,

103
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:16,710
but I lost sight of him.

104
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,090
[PROPERTY OFFICER] Hmm?

105
00:06:18,210 --> 00:06:19,670
By the way, sir,

106
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:22,220
I have been looking
for a lost slave for some time.

107
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:23,300
[PROPERTY OFFICER] Huh?

108
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,260
Do you happen to have any girls
who resemble her

109
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:27,390
and are subjects
of Prince Chagatai?

110
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:31,230
Hmm. A slave from the West
belonging to the prince.

111
00:06:31,350 --> 00:06:34,520
[Sitara grunts] No chance
you'll find one that easily.

112
00:06:34,650 --> 00:06:38,230
[grunts] Yesterday,
I took in three such slaves.

113
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:39,400
[SITARA] Huh?

114
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,240
After the Kurultai,

115
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:44,450
I have quite a few
who appear to be lost now.

116
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,570
If you squint just a little bit,

117
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:48,740
you might say this girl
resembles her, I suppose.

118
00:06:48,870 --> 00:06:51,950
[SHIRA] Yes, of course.
[laughs] There you are.

119
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,870
You two look so alike.

120
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,580
Huh... Not one bit.

121
00:06:56,710 --> 00:06:58,300
[SITARA]
You can say that again.

122
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,460
So long, and good luck to you.

123
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:02,840
I hope you manage
to find your master soon.

124
00:07:02,970 --> 00:07:05,090
-[FEMALE SLAVE] Not one bit.
-[SITARA] Thanks a lot.

125
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:06,470
-[grunts]
-Well,

126
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,890
we'd better have you wait here
with the other girls.

127
00:07:09,010 --> 00:07:10,970
I'm sure someone will come soon.

128
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,350
[Sitara scoffs]

129
00:07:15,730 --> 00:07:18,690
[SITARA] There are more
lost people than I'd imagined.

130
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:21,690
Hold on, I wonder if they...

131
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:24,900
Um, excuse me,
do you speak Persian?

132
00:07:25,030 --> 00:07:26,200
[BOTH] Huh?

133
00:07:26,410 --> 00:07:27,660
We do.

134
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:29,700
♪

135
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:31,660
[SITARA] Wow. Really?

136
00:07:31,790 --> 00:07:34,040
You two are
from Mashhad and Merv?

137
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,540
I hail from Tus.

138
00:07:35,670 --> 00:07:36,830
I know it quite well.

139
00:07:36,920 --> 00:07:39,380
It is a city I'd always hoped
to visit one day.

140
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,960
Oh, is that true?

141
00:07:41,090 --> 00:07:43,550
I was told it was
bustling with many people

142
00:07:43,670 --> 00:07:44,880
and very lively.

143
00:07:45,010 --> 00:07:46,380
Yes, absolutely.

144
00:07:47,010 --> 00:07:49,930
One of the liveliest places
I've seen.

145
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:51,720
And who knows?

146
00:07:51,810 --> 00:07:54,270
Perhaps we would have
come across each other sometime.

147
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:57,690
[SLAVES] Yes.

148
00:07:58,690 --> 00:08:00,560
[SLAVE 1]
I remember those days.

149
00:08:00,690 --> 00:08:04,030
Shopping at the bazaar
was something I truly loved.

150
00:08:07,950 --> 00:08:10,950
[SLAVE 2] I'm serving
Prince Chagatai's family now.

151
00:08:11,580 --> 00:08:14,540
But somehow,
I managed to lose my way,

152
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,750
and I feel worried
about my own family.

153
00:08:16,870 --> 00:08:18,000
Your family is here?

154
00:08:18,130 --> 00:08:21,250
They are. My husband
is a slave just like me.

155
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:22,500
He was born in Bukhara

156
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:24,840
and is quite
a skilled craftsman.

157
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:27,760
When they first brought us
out here to Mongolia,

158
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:29,930
I felt so scared and hopeless.

159
00:08:30,050 --> 00:08:32,310
But now I have my husband
and our children.

160
00:08:32,430 --> 00:08:34,890
Honestly, I never
could have imagined

161
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:36,390
how well my life would turn out.

162
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:38,560
Well, home is where you make it.

163
00:08:38,940 --> 00:08:42,570
And Prince Chagatai's ulus
is a very peaceful one at that,

164
00:08:42,690 --> 00:08:44,230
so I feel truly grateful.

165
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,030
[SITARA] There are people
who have come here

166
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:48,780
and found whole new lives
for themselves.

167
00:08:48,990 --> 00:08:50,530
[gasps, grunts]

168
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:52,120
I mustn't.

169
00:08:52,870 --> 00:08:56,660
At times, I feel myself
about to forgive them.

170
00:08:57,120 --> 00:09:01,040
But then I remember...
the vow that I made

171
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:05,960
to never forget what
the Mongols did to all of us.

172
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:09,800
[PROPERTY OFFICER]
Hey, the girl who just arrived.

173
00:09:09,930 --> 00:09:11,300
Do you mean me, sir?

174
00:09:11,430 --> 00:09:13,890
That's right.
Come along with me.

175
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:17,310
[SITARA] Uh...

176
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:19,980
Did Shira already get someone
to come after me?

177
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,520
That was really fast.

178
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:31,370
Here is who you asked for.
This is the girl.

179
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:33,990
I've been told you've got
a Jada stone.

180
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,370
-Uh, yes.
-Show me.

181
00:09:39,290 --> 00:09:41,540
Why do you want it?

182
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,040
[grunts]

183
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:45,550
-[Sitara gasps]
-Come.

184
00:09:45,670 --> 00:09:47,090
[Sitara stutters] Uh... What?

185
00:09:47,210 --> 00:09:49,050
-[MAN] Get up there.
-[Sitara grunts]

186
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:52,470
[SITARA] What's happening?
It's as if he's...

187
00:09:52,590 --> 00:09:54,970
-You're a big girl.
-Huh?

188
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,600
-Don't run away, you thief.
-Huh?

189
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:58,770
[MAN] Chuu!

190
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:01,060
[Sitara screaming]

191
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:05,150
Did you just say I was a thief?
There must be some mistake.

192
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:06,480
Who are you?

193
00:10:06,610 --> 00:10:08,440
You're not
one of Prince Chagatai's men

194
00:10:08,570 --> 00:10:10,150
-who's taking me back.
-[grunts]

195
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:12,200
If I say camel, you say goat.

196
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,610
Huh? What's that?

197
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:16,370
In other words,
you are completely mistaken.

198
00:10:16,490 --> 00:10:18,910
Just give it up and start
confessing your crimes.

199
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,910
What do you mean?
I haven't done--

200
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:23,830
-Chuu!
-[Sitara cries]

201
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,210
[MAN] Chuu! Chuu!

202
00:10:30,510 --> 00:10:33,050
[Sitara groans] That hurts.

203
00:10:33,180 --> 00:10:35,140
Where are you
taking me right now?

204
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,390
-Be quiet. Just follow me.
-[cries]

205
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,640
It's Qadaq.
Pardon the intrusion.

206
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:45,270
I found the girl
who stole the stone.

207
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:46,440
She's outside.

208
00:10:46,570 --> 00:10:48,440
[SITARA] Hold on.
I haven't stolen anything.

209
00:10:48,570 --> 00:10:50,570
-Get in here now.
-[SITARA] What?

210
00:10:51,490 --> 00:10:52,650
[Sitara grunts]

211
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:56,030
[WOMAN] Good work
bringing her here, Qadaq.

212
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,030
[Sitara gasps]

213
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,620
♪

214
00:11:04,790 --> 00:11:06,540
Uh... [gasps]

215
00:11:07,710 --> 00:11:09,210
[SITARA] It's that woman.

216
00:11:11,260 --> 00:11:12,420
So it was you.

217
00:11:13,760 --> 00:11:16,850
You were the one who stole
my Jada stone from me.

218
00:11:17,050 --> 00:11:18,260
What are you talking about?

219
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:20,430
-Don't lie to me!
-[whimpers]

220
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:21,850
Yes, that's it.

221
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:23,850
Ögedei ordered you to,
didn't he?

222
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:27,230
Does he intend to deprive me
of everything I care for?

223
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:29,860
-[breathes heavily]
-Uh, my apologies,

224
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,360
but may I ask
who you are exactly?

225
00:11:32,490 --> 00:11:33,780
I fear there's been
a grave error--

226
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,820
Do you not know
to whom you kneel?

227
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:40,990
This is Töregene Khatun,
sixth wife of Ögedei Kha'an.

228
00:11:41,410 --> 00:11:42,790
[exhales sharply]

229
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,330
[Sitara gasps]

230
00:11:45,460 --> 00:11:48,790
[SITARA] The Great Kha'an's
sixth wife?

231
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:51,460
[breathing heavily]

232
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:56,130
[SITARA]
I finally see what's going on.

233
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:58,510
I've been brought
to Ögedei's ulus

234
00:11:58,640 --> 00:12:00,850
after being mistaken
for a thief.

235
00:12:01,310 --> 00:12:03,560
What a terrifying predicament!

236
00:12:03,850 --> 00:12:05,310
No more lies.

237
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:08,940
You stole my Jada stone,
didn't you? Give it back!

238
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:10,480
[Sitara gasps]

239
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,480
[SITARA] A Jada stone...

240
00:12:12,610 --> 00:12:16,610
In my homeland, it's treasured
for its medicinal properties.

241
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:18,870
But here, if I recall...

242
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,950
[PROPERTY OFFICER]
When a kam soaks one in water,

243
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:26,620
it is said to immediately
bring forth a mighty rainstorm.

244
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,290
I'm certain she must have had
her own Jada stone

245
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:30,840
and lost it at some point.

246
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,590
That's why she thinks
the one I have

247
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:33,920
was stolen from her.

248
00:12:34,300 --> 00:12:36,800
In that case,
if I show her my stone,

249
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:39,180
she should realize
it's different from hers.

250
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:40,720
[gasps]

251
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:43,930
But would she truly be able
to tell the difference

252
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:46,810
between these stones?
What if they look the same?

253
00:12:46,930 --> 00:12:49,190
So it was you
who stole it after all!

254
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,520
-Die!
-[whimpers]

255
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:54,740
[SITARA] But still...

256
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:58,240
What are you doing, girl?
Give the stone back already.

257
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:03,780
[SITARA] No choice.
I just have to show it to her.

258
00:13:08,580 --> 00:13:10,040
[gasps softly] That's not it.

259
00:13:10,170 --> 00:13:11,130
[Sitara gasps]

260
00:13:11,880 --> 00:13:14,090
My stone
is a bit smaller than that,

261
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:16,000
and it has
a more pleasing shape.

262
00:13:16,130 --> 00:13:17,090
Huh?

263
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:19,930
Yes, I promise you,
I found this stone myself.

264
00:13:21,470 --> 00:13:23,800
Qadaq, what are you playing at?

265
00:13:23,930 --> 00:13:25,010
[QADAQ] Um...

266
00:13:25,470 --> 00:13:28,480
Sorry. Seems we had
the wrong person.

267
00:13:28,600 --> 00:13:29,890
[grunts]

268
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,650
[TÖREGENE] That's enough.

269
00:13:32,770 --> 00:13:35,020
You've displeased me.
Leave at once.

270
00:13:35,610 --> 00:13:37,780
[both hesitate]

271
00:13:38,530 --> 00:13:41,490
Well, didn't you hear her?
Get out already.

272
00:13:43,450 --> 00:13:45,620
So then,
what am I supposed to do now?

273
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:48,040
What? You're not needed here.
Begone.

274
00:13:48,160 --> 00:13:50,290
Not needed here?
I'll have you know

275
00:13:50,410 --> 00:13:51,630
-I'm a lost slave.
-[MEN] Huh?

276
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:54,210
I have no idea
how to get back to my camp.

277
00:13:54,340 --> 00:13:56,590
And it looks like
it's getting darker.

278
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:58,920
[cries] Oh, no!

279
00:13:59,050 --> 00:14:01,180
-It's too scary.
-Hey.

280
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:03,350
Somebody help me!

281
00:14:03,470 --> 00:14:04,890
I was forcibly abducted

282
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:07,520
by Lady Töregene's retainer,
Qadaq--

283
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:10,520
Hey, quiet down. Fine then.

284
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,020
I'll take you to the tent
where I found you tomorrow.

285
00:14:13,150 --> 00:14:14,900
-Tomorrow?
-[groans]

286
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:17,860
You can stay the night here,
so just follow me.

287
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,280
Oh, yeah, and one more thing,

288
00:14:25,410 --> 00:14:27,790
I am not Lady Töregene's
retainer, you know.

289
00:14:28,290 --> 00:14:29,750
It's a bit of a long story,

290
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:32,040
but I'm acting
on someone else's orders.

291
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:34,080
-[Sitara gasps]
-It's true.

292
00:14:34,210 --> 00:14:37,550
I can't tell you whose, though.
I must keep that a secret.

293
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:39,960
It's at their behest
that I serve

294
00:14:40,090 --> 00:14:43,050
at Lady Töregene's side
for the foreseeable future.

295
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:44,680
Huh?

296
00:14:45,850 --> 00:14:47,100
She's gone?

297
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:53,640
[SITARA] Those are...

298
00:14:53,940 --> 00:14:55,810
[laughing]

299
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,900
[laughing]

300
00:15:01,110 --> 00:15:02,320
How about that?

301
00:15:02,450 --> 00:15:04,870
You may be the Great Kha'an
now, Ögedei,

302
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:07,740
but you're still no match
for me on the back of a horse.

303
00:15:07,870 --> 00:15:09,620
[ÖGEDEI] I applaud your skills.

304
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:11,330
How very amusing.

305
00:15:11,450 --> 00:15:14,040
It's so rare to see you more
drunk than me, Chagatai.

306
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,250
And how could I
not drink right now?

307
00:15:16,380 --> 00:15:19,380
My beloved little brother has
officially been crowned emperor.

308
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:21,800
Could there ever be
a more festive occasion?

309
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,300
You still haven't drunk enough?

310
00:15:24,220 --> 00:15:27,140
[SITARA] Prince Chagatai
and Ögedei Kha'an?

311
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,350
What could they be
talking about?

312
00:15:29,470 --> 00:15:31,390
-I can't hear them very well.
-[clattering]

313
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:34,980
-[Sitara gasps]
-Huh? Who dares intrude on us?

314
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,230
Seize the scoundrel immediately!

315
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:38,770
-[VASSAL 1] Right.
-[VASSAL 2] Get her!

316
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,780
[grunts, whimpers]

317
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:43,450
[KIRGISTANI]
You, suspicious girl,

318
00:15:43,570 --> 00:15:45,860
what were you doing
back there, hm?

319
00:15:45,990 --> 00:15:47,660
Huh? Isn't she
one of our slaves?

320
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:50,200
I don't recall
ever seeing her before.

321
00:15:50,330 --> 00:15:51,990
Perhaps she's here to spy on us.

322
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:53,410
[Sitara gasps]

323
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:55,960
[SITARA] Why must everything
go wrong today?

324
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:59,000
[ÖGEDEI] Is something the
matter? Kirgistani? Möge?

325
00:15:59,130 --> 00:16:01,590
Wait, Great Kha'an!
you must keep your distance.

326
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,800
We've restrained someone
that could be dangerous.

327
00:16:03,920 --> 00:16:05,510
Someone dangerous?

328
00:16:05,630 --> 00:16:07,640
Let us see
what she has to say first.

329
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:10,640
Now then, who are you?

330
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:11,720
Uh...

331
00:16:13,010 --> 00:16:15,600
[SITARA]
So this is Ögedei Kha'an...

332
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:19,110
the new Mongol emperor.

333
00:16:21,360 --> 00:16:23,320
-[QADAQ] Huh? Huh?
-[TÖREGENE] She disappeared?

334
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,900
Yes, around here.

335
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:26,530
Lady Töregene,

336
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:29,120
I believe there is something odd
about that slave,

337
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,370
and I have news to share.

338
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:35,580
[Töregene gasps] Ögedei.

339
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:37,250
Hmm.

340
00:16:38,460 --> 00:16:40,960
So, who is the master you serve?

341
00:16:41,090 --> 00:16:43,130
My master? [grunts]

342
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:46,880
Right now, it's supposed
to be Prince Chagatai.

343
00:16:47,010 --> 00:16:50,760
But if I say that, it'll only
complicate things further.

344
00:16:50,890 --> 00:16:52,390
What answer should I give?

345
00:16:52,510 --> 00:16:54,850
Go on, out with it already.

346
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:59,020
Um, Empress Töregene
is my mistress.

347
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:02,020
-[both gasp]
-Why would she say that?

348
00:17:02,150 --> 00:17:03,270
[Töregene grunts]

349
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:06,740
-Töregene?
-Well, that sounds plausible.

350
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:09,530
Ögedei, you give
that troublesome woman

351
00:17:09,660 --> 00:17:11,030
far too much freedom.

352
00:17:11,160 --> 00:17:13,080
-[ÖGEDEI] Hmm.
-You there, girl,

353
00:17:13,540 --> 00:17:15,700
I don't know what
Töregene asked of you,

354
00:17:15,830 --> 00:17:17,830
but you'd do well
to stop your prowling.

355
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:19,500
Obey the law.

356
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:21,080
You're a woman and a slave.

357
00:17:21,210 --> 00:17:22,630
You should know
better than that.

358
00:17:23,590 --> 00:17:24,840
You Muslims,

359
00:17:25,050 --> 00:17:27,880
you all have a vexing tendency
to disobey all our laws,

360
00:17:28,010 --> 00:17:30,680
cutting the throats of sheep
and bathing in rivers.

361
00:17:31,550 --> 00:17:35,560
Why must you weaklings insist on
bringing ruin upon yourselves?

362
00:17:40,690 --> 00:17:41,730
I'm quite certain...

363
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:43,230
[scoffs] Hmm?

364
00:17:44,110 --> 00:17:47,990
I'm quite certain you could
never understand, Your Highness.

365
00:17:48,110 --> 00:17:50,110
[gasps, breathes shakily]

366
00:17:51,450 --> 00:17:53,200
♪

367
00:17:53,950 --> 00:17:55,790
Hmm. [exhales]

368
00:17:58,950 --> 00:18:00,920
Huh? [grunts]

369
00:18:01,710 --> 00:18:04,920
-Huh? Oh, Töregene is here now.
-[Sitara gasps]

370
00:18:05,050 --> 00:18:08,340
Listen up, this young girl
claims to be one of your slaves.

371
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:09,510
So is it true?

372
00:18:12,090 --> 00:18:13,340
[SITARA] I'm done for.

373
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,600
-[Sitara whimpers]
-[TÖREGENE] Hmm.

374
00:18:16,010 --> 00:18:18,470
How clumsy
to let yourself be caught.

375
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:20,180
-[SITARA] Uh...
-[KIRGISTANI] Huh?

376
00:18:20,890 --> 00:18:22,520
[TÖREGENE] Yes, it's true.

377
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,060
[all gasp]

378
00:18:25,230 --> 00:18:28,570
I ordered this girl to come here
and assassinate you,

379
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:30,740
Great Kha'an.

380
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:36,120
[chuckles]
I guess that's that then.

381
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,160
[both gasp]

382
00:18:37,290 --> 00:18:39,790
All right,
your ploy has been exposed.

383
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:41,410
You're all free to disperse now.

384
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:42,500
Great Kha'an!

385
00:18:42,870 --> 00:18:45,460
Looking lovely tonight,
Kirgistani.

386
00:18:45,590 --> 00:18:46,800
[both gasp]

387
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,880
My Möge, sleep well.

388
00:18:49,010 --> 00:18:51,090
[Möge chuckles] Yes.

389
00:18:51,210 --> 00:18:52,300
[sighs]

390
00:18:53,510 --> 00:18:54,970
You too, Töregene.

391
00:18:55,220 --> 00:18:56,390
[Töregene scoffs]

392
00:18:56,890 --> 00:19:01,350
[Kirgistani grunts,
scoffs, grumbles]

393
00:19:04,650 --> 00:19:05,770
[SITARA] Uh...

394
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:09,070
Ögedei, why are you so--

395
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:11,360
That's enough now.
It's time to head back.

396
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:14,950
People will begin to worry
if you're not home soon.

397
00:19:18,660 --> 00:19:20,540
You're so
kind-hearted, Chagatai.

398
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:23,370
-What now?
-You had said before,

399
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:25,920
as the Mongol Empire expands,

400
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:27,920
it becomes a massive throng
of people

401
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:30,250
following different customs
and faiths.

402
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:33,670
The first ones to suffer from
their conflicts will be women,

403
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:36,180
slaves, and the weak.

404
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:38,180
Hmm.

405
00:19:38,970 --> 00:19:41,020
[ÖGEDEI]
However, if we properly spread

406
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,350
the laws of Genghis Khan,

407
00:19:42,470 --> 00:19:45,310
they can be protected,
even the weak.

408
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,650
Guilty.

409
00:19:46,940 --> 00:19:48,190
Can't they?

410
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:49,570
[Chagatai grunts]

411
00:19:50,150 --> 00:19:51,570
I'm leaving.

412
00:19:55,530 --> 00:19:57,910
[ÖGEDEI]
You are truly so caring.

413
00:19:58,410 --> 00:20:02,290
Sadly, not everybody is
as wise as you.

414
00:20:02,370 --> 00:20:03,870
Some are not so capable

415
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,540
of grasping
their own standing so clearly.

416
00:20:06,670 --> 00:20:09,790
And there are some things
that simply cannot be changed.

417
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,420
♪

418
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:18,720
That is all now. You may leave.

419
00:20:18,850 --> 00:20:20,220
Yes, ma'am.

420
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:23,600
[Qadaq sighs]

421
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:33,610
Sorry, but why exactly did you
decide to come to my aid?

422
00:20:33,730 --> 00:20:34,780
[TÖREGENE] Hmm.

423
00:20:35,030 --> 00:20:37,450
I simply took a liking
to your smile.

424
00:20:37,570 --> 00:20:38,660
[Sitara gasps]

425
00:20:38,870 --> 00:20:42,450
Tell me, girl, you appear
to be Persian, correct?

426
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:43,910
Uh, yes.

427
00:20:44,040 --> 00:20:46,830
Do you hate them, the Mongols?

428
00:20:46,960 --> 00:20:48,330
[Sitara breathes uneasily]

429
00:20:50,130 --> 00:20:51,840
Answer me honestly.

430
00:20:52,130 --> 00:20:54,250
I promise I won't tell anyone.

431
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,380
[gasps]

432
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:58,720
Actually,
you were there earlier.

433
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:01,050
You already know
how they treat me.

434
00:21:01,180 --> 00:21:02,510
Even if I told them,

435
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:05,470
nobody would take me
at my word anyway.

436
00:21:06,140 --> 00:21:07,810
Do you hate them?

437
00:21:08,060 --> 00:21:10,310
[Sitara gasps,
breathes uneasily]

438
00:21:13,270 --> 00:21:15,320
[SITARA]
They took everything from me.

439
00:21:15,650 --> 00:21:17,190
I cannot forgive them.

440
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:21,120
I... I refuse
to ever let myself.

441
00:21:21,700 --> 00:21:23,030
[Sitara breathes heavily]

442
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:25,490
[Töregene sighs]

443
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:29,250
[TÖREGENE]
Even so, as time passes,

444
00:21:29,370 --> 00:21:32,130
you feel yourself almost
forgiving them. Am I wrong?

445
00:21:32,250 --> 00:21:34,290
[Sitara gasps] Lady Töregene,

446
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,710
could it be?

447
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:38,970
[Töregene exhales]

448
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:53,520
Do you think you'd be willing
to hear my tale?

449
00:21:53,650 --> 00:21:54,820
♪

450
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:04,660
[♪ closing theme song playing]

451
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:35,410
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Next time, "The Mergen People."

